    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0275" n="1109" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/217</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schmedeman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>202. With reference to Legation’s No. 440 of December 30, the War Trade Board are
                    unanimous in their feeling that the proposal to Nansen of December 20 is
                    eminently fair and reasonable and must stand.</p>
                <p>Referring to Legation’s No. 445 of January 3, the proposal of December 20 to
                        Nansen itself
                    contains the best statement of the attitude and demands of United States and
                    needs no amplification <pb facs="0276" n="1110" xml:id="pg1110"/> or discussion,
                    and you are instructed to publish full text of this proposal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
